/*  EXPECTED: REJECTED at type-check, identically by both backends.

    Written to attack the store rules (2026-11-17 review): for each rabbit rows into outer. A rabbit's series reaches
    something that outlives the rabbit (docs/SOUNDNESS.md, obligation O2). */

Define outer as a series of series of number.
Pull a rabbit.
    Define inner-table as a series of series of number.
    Insert (a series of number with (1, 2, 3)) into inner-table.
    For each row in inner-table, repeat:
        Insert row into outer.
    Done.
Done.

Define churn as a series of text.
Define tick as 0.
While tick is less than 400, repeat:
    Insert ("zzzzzzzz" joined to "yyyyyyyy") into churn.
    tick becomes tick + 1.
Done.
State outer.
